      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "7d3a26ba55d12ab131244415d19a354a",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"urbanfeather-local-pbf-pipeline\">UrbanFEATHER local-PBF pipeline</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This notebook has four stages:</span>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Config</strong> - read places, FEATHER parameters, and OSM amenity categories.</li>\n<li><strong>Local OSM data</strong> - choose a Geofabrik extract, clip a city PBF, build the walking graph, and extract POIs.</li>\n<li><strong>FEATHER features</strong> - calculate each node's network distance to the nearest POI in every category and pass those raw metre values directly into the sine/cosine transform.</li>\n<li><strong>Output</strong> - run <code>FEATHER_new</code>, save one embedding CSV per city, and inspect the results on the street graph.</li>\n</ol>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The workbook runs automatically when opened. Expensive reusable OSM/graph results are cached under <code>../cache/</code>; raw-metre FEATHER CSV files are written to <code>../output/FEATHER_embeddings_raw_meters/</code>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
