          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"characteristic-function-explorer\">Characteristic-function explorer</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The original FEATHER <code>charfun.jpg</code> plots characteristic-function values against the evaluation point <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\theta||)</marimo-tex>.\nIts two lines are class-wise means and the shaded areas are one standard deviation around those means.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">This urban version uses the same idea. Because the street-network data has no \"popular/unpopular\" class label,\nit compares two groups for the selected amenity category:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>closest nodes</strong>: the selected fraction of nodes with the shortest network distance to the amenity;</li>\n<li><strong>farthest nodes</strong>: the same fraction with the largest network distance.</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">In this workbook FEATHER receives raw nearest-amenity distances in metres, so the sine/cosine phase is <code>theta * distance_m</code> with no 20 km scaling.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The plot reads only the required columns from an existing FEATHER CSV.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
